drm/etnaviv: return from the cmdbuf space wait when a signal is pending

etnaviv_cmdbuf_init() waits with wait_event_interruptible_timeout() when
the suballocator is full and gives up only when it returns 0.  With a
signal pending the wait returns -ERESTARTSYS at once, and the code goes
back to retry.  Once the region stays full, the task spins in the submit
ioctl for good: a fatal signal can never be delivered, kill -9 does
nothing, and the only way out is a reboot.

Seen on a Pyra (OMAP5432, GC320 2D core) after an HDMI hotplug under the
armsoc X driver: the 2D core took an MMU fault, "recover hung GPU!"
followed, and Xorg then sat in R state at about 85 % system time with
SIGKILL pending, every sysrq backtrace in etnaviv_ioctl_gem_submit ->
etnaviv_cmdbuf_init.

Return the error.  Nothing has been committed at that point and the
submit is put on the error path, so the ioctl can be restarted.  This
relies on the previous patch, which keeps the cleanup from freeing
granules the cmdbuf never got.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_cmdbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_cmdbuf.c
@@ -105,6 +105,8 @@ retry:
 				"Timeout waiting for cmdbuf space\n");
 			return -ETIMEDOUT;
 		}
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
 		goto retry;
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&suballoc->lock);
